{ +same thing. } ) 2. Qf3+ Rg2 3. Qd1+ Rg1 4. Qf3+ Qg2 5. Qh5+ Qh2 $10
{ +[Drawn. Queen and Pawn against Queen should be drawn in the majority of cases, because the player with the Pawn can rarely find sufficient cover for his King and yet support the advance of his Pawn. In the present instance he apparently succeeded in both objects and yet only draws; but such instances occur with the h-Pawn (or a-Pawn) and g-Pawn (or b-Pawn) only. The King of the weaker side must be kept at a distance from the Pawn.] }
